[Event "Sample basics"]
[Lesson "weak-f7"]
[LessonTitle "The weak f7 square"]
[Step "explain"]
[TeacherNotes "At the start, f7 is guarded only by the king | Two attackers on f7 can win quickly"]
[Mistakes "Moving the queen out too early without a plan"]
[ClassQuestions "Which black piece guards f7 at the start?"]

{Watch how White aims two pieces at the f7 pawn. [%csl Rf7] [%cal Gd1h5,Gf1c4]}
1. e4 e5 2. Qh5 {The queen eyes f7 and the e5 pawn. [%cal Gh5f7]} 2... Nc6
3. Bc4 {Now the bishop and queen both attack f7. [%cal Gc4f7,Gh5f7]} 3... Nf6?
4. Qxf7# {The queen takes f7 and the king has no escape. [%csl Rf7,Re8]} 1-0

[Event "Sample basics"]
[Lesson "weak-f7"]
[Step "find-move"]
[FEN "r1bqkb1r/pppp1ppp/2n2n2/4p2Q/2B1P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNB1K1NR w KQkq - 4 4"]
[Hint "Use your queen."]
[Hint "Look at the f7 square."]

{White to move. Find the strongest move.}
4. Qxf7# {Checkmate.} 1-0

[Event "Sample basics"]
[Lesson "weak-f7"]
[Step "line-drill"]
[Side "white"]
[Hint "Develop the queen toward the f7 pawn."]

{Play the quick attack as White.}
1. e4 e5 2. Qh5 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. Qxf7# *

[Event "Sample basics"]
[Lesson "weak-f7"]
[Step "explain"]

{The queen and the bishop both attack f7, and only the king guards it.}
1. e4 e5 2. Qh5 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 *
